   - Engine asymmetry: QEMU `-cpu andes-ax45mpv` advertises RVS|RVU (S/U-capable); the default RTL `ax45mpv_premium` is M-only (`NDS_NUM_PRIVILEGE_LEVELS 1`). The S/U engine is `ax66_makatau` (paired with `-cpu andes-ax66`).
   - --verify: re-runs ELF on pure-QEMU oracle, diffs full drained state via `diff_states`. Two policies: hybrid (`compare_trap_cause=false`) and lock-step DV (`compare_trap_cause=true`).
   - Limitation IDs L1–L24 in docs/andes_sim_limitations.ipynb. This work added L24.
   - TDD via doctest (hybrid unit tests, host-buildable with g++) + custom test_check.hpp harness (driver tests).
   - vsim build is podman-based (`scripts/build_vsim.sh`, ~30s incremental for header-only changes). Driver build = `scripts/build_driver.sh` (cmake, also runs ctest). Header-only hybrid `.hpp` changes compile into vsim's main.cpp.

